  "id": "commonality-analysis",
  "term": "commonality analysis",
  "definition": "Commonality analysis is a way of examining how several factors relate to an outcome by separating what each factor contributes on its own from what it shares with other factors. In psychology research, it can be used to estimate the relative importance of different stressors and their overlapping links with well-being.",
